title: The 'Potempa Five' Are Pardoned!
subtitle: Murder excused in the name of politics.
view-if: chancellor = "Goodryke" and papen_time == 13 and potempa_five_convicted and heartland_leader == "Goodryke"
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/potempa5.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

= The 'Potempa Five' Are Pardoned!

In a bid to win <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> support for his government, Goodryke and his Justice Minister have bowed to pressure and commuted the murderers' sentences, using his power as Heartland's <i>Commonwealth Commissioner</i>. The hope is that the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> will back Goodryke in the upcoming confidence vote—but this capitulation has only strengthened the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, laying bare the government's unwillingness—or inability—to confront them.

- @papen

@papen
title: Shameful.
on-arrival: pro_republic -= 3; burgher_royalist -= 2; guild_royalist -= 2; landed_royalist -= 2; loyalist_militancy += 0.02; loyalist_strength += 50

Yet another disgraceful capitulation to the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>. Still, their shameless defense of convicted murderers may alienate voters and cost them dearly at the next election.